{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for sales-design draft9 6d10f57d5bdc28627a2994e052f06a2f7c2489fc / tree a93f87501b0e534c5c911609fe98256473962199, primary984d469c, notes/2026-10-19-sales-applications-design.md. Full435-line primary read first. The two calendar corrections from8f620cba are resolved; the rewrite has one lost bid safeguard and new factual problems in the market comparison.\n\nResolved F3/F5 calendar: refused is declared; admission outcomes are pending/admitted/refused/superseded, with superseded returning the post to approved. Admission remains separate from a member's receipt check and from native completion, which is deferred. One quarter with at most24 posts including retired, whole queried rows at most6KiB and text at most4KiB gives at most147456bytes (144KiB) before bounded envelope overhead, comfortably below256KiB. This is a design constraint for future enforcement, not runtime acceptance. No larger native limit is needed.\n\nF2 regression, medium — Restore the current-assembly check at submit (section6 lines280–288). Draft8 expressly said an assembly made stale by any later change cannot be submitted; draft9 checks current approvals and rendering only at assemble, then says management seals that exact assembly. Counterexample: assemble at price revision A with granted approval; supply price B, which resets approval to requested; submit the unchanged assembly A. Checking the assembly's own revision does not check its other items. State briefly that submit refuses unless its rendering, all answer revisions and both approvals still match the current complete response. Keep the old assembly immutable. Retain the existing one-approval-per-kind and assigned-reviewer guard when a reviewer is set; the shorter note need not restore the old definitions catalogue. C3 should include refusal of this changed-after-assembly case. These are retained constraints, not a new feature request.\n\nF6, medium — Correct current-product claims and narrow the claimed differences in sections2–3:\n• Lines125–130 say contributors must go to an RFP portal and contrast this with working from their own AI app. Loopio's current product page explicitly supports SMEs answering in Slack/Teams, and its Copilot Agent lets SMEs create library entries from Teams/M365 Copilot. Acknowledge that overlap; the proposed member signatures, journal and grant model may still be a difference, without claiming exclusive in-app access. Primary sources: https://loopio.com/ (collaboration FAQ); https://support.loopio.com/hc/en-us/articles/43969095406867-What-is-the-Loopio-Copilot-Agent-for-Microsoft-365 .\n• Lines152–155 present approval of the exact published text as the calendar's difference. Planable already documents approved content becoming read-only until an approver unapproves it, with required approval before scheduled publication and version history. Acknowledge that feature and describe the proposed signed/replayable record and repository publication specifically, rather than implying other calendars cannot preserve approved copy. https://planable.io/guides/content-approvals-in-planable/ (approval flow, lock after approval, version history).\n• Lines134–140 list Relay as a current outreach option. Its live official site says it shut down in September2026 and its accounts/workflows/history were deleted. Remove it from the current list or label it historical. The indexed old docs still describe HITL steps but now redirect to the shutdown notice: https://relay.app/ .\n• Lines99–106 make universal claims that an agent's approval is a transcript held only by that agent and its schedule only a promise to itself. Those claims are unsupported by the named products: OpenAI documents user-visible activity, custom authorization rules and action review; Meta documents a user-visible audit trail. Frame the room's exact shared facts, independent members and replayable rules as proposed guarantees, not as proof that agents lack auditable approvals or real schedulers. Also qualify “Every one ... database the seller maintains”: Attio documents automatic record creation, enrichment and email/calendar sync. https://openai.com/index/introducing-dots/ ; https://about.fb.com/news/2026/09/introducing-muse-personal-ai-agent/ ; https://attio.com/help/reference/email-calendar/email-and-calendar-syncing .\n\nThe Dots/Muse launch dates and broad capability summaries are supported by the official launch pages; Hermes's persistent memory, skills, scheduling and messaging by https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs . Primary links would make these claims easier to verify than the Vellum summaries. Rankings/pricing are not independently endorsed.\n\nArchitecture conclusion: the bounded calendar, fixed-domain bid supply, separate approval openings, complete-or-refused assembly,50-row/2KiB bid bounds and64KiB rendering fit the previously checked landed forms. Restore the cross-item freshness guard at submission. No native completion/pagination/deletion capability is assumed.\nSecurity conclusion: expert supply and team review retain attribution; buyer remains outside; hosted agents/custody remain deferred. The admission/member-check boundary is sound. Sealing stale answers after approval reset must remain refused.\nSimplification conclusion: the shorter note is useful. Keep its structure, add a short retained-guards sentence, and make the comparison factual with primary sources and acknowledged overlap. No implementation is commissioned; C1–C4 remain after plan033. Owner-read landing hold in29c1acab is acknowledged.\n\nValidation: only this Markdown path differs from Main2127; whitespace clean; all6 local links/fragments resolve. PrimarySHA256 15a9018e1fda54bb6c2fdf0fe56b31690b2b4b5f1e914444255ad2a2b5ba303f. Scratch /private/tmp/checker-sales-design-jne3y8sq retains draft9-primary.md, draft8-to9.diff and draft9-validation.json. Native prepare correctly binds implementation7f569087/promise28988cd9/current report984d469c at this head. Prior unchanged contract/judge/Result/query/publication source checks reused. Official live product pages checked today; no source/test edits, tests/gate rerun, package installation, push or deployment.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:984d469c4ab1d61a7d157d5f97f027367ff351cb","binding":"assigned","head":"6d10f57d5bdc28627a2994e052f06a2f7c2489fc","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:050cc438e7dc703caa4dea6ff75d17be862ff90c\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:28988cd98dfb9eddaadb8934b253cc352c17814f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:29c1acab0edf185858348391d56ce6cfc9e6e17d","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}